    "## Atomic \xe2\x80\x94 lock-free shared state\n"
    "`Atomic<T>` wraps `int`, `float`, or `bool` with C11 atomic operations. Must be declared `shared`; `move` prohibited.\n"
    "\n"
    "Methods: `load`, `store`, `add`, `sub`, `fetchAdd`, `fetchSub`, `swap`, `compareExchange`, `toggle`, `toString`.\n"
    "\n"
    "All methods accept optional `Ordering` enum (default `SeqCst`): `Relaxed`, `Acquire`, `Release`, `AcquireRelease`, `SeqCst`.\n"
    "\n"
    "```xray\n"
    "shared counter = Atomic(0)\n"
    "counter.add(1)\n"
    "var (old, ok) = counter.compareExchange(1, 42)\n"
    "print(counter.load())  // 42\n"
    "```\n"
    "\n"
    "## Locks \xe2\x80\x94 explicit execution domain\n"
    "`sync.*` locks are coroutine-domain primitives: they may suspend and require `import sync`. `sys.Os*` locks are OS-thread-domain primitives: they block the current OS thread and require `import sys`. Synchronization handles must be created with `shared` when named.\n"
    "\n"
    "```xray\n"
    "import sync\n"
    "import sys\n"
    "\n"
    "shared m = sync.Mutex<int>(0)\n"
    "shared os_m = sys.OsMutex()\n"
    "```\n"
    "";

